# Wave W17-T (Route 134): gate sand — delivery-channel sand: a warm bright shore sand where the three rivers of sea converge and deliver east to Perennial — pale delivery flecks standing in the tread, the last shore of the fastest water (design: three rivers becoming one delivery at the falls\u2019 foot; Perennial\u2019s falls are the town-side frame, byte-preserved; the shipped current cells are mechanic data, byte-identical entire). Route 134\u2019s own sand — the warmest and brightest of the three current shores: split from Route 133\u2019s cool hard-foamed rapid sand by temperature and foam (delivery flecks vs rapid dashes) and from Route 130\u2019s garden-flecked quiet sand by the missing garden colours (the quiet water is behind; this shore faces the falls).
